# text = I am informed that the cost of equipping mines with these alarms can be gathered from the fact that an average mine employing 1,000 men underground can be equipped at an addition to the wage bill of a miserable £ 3 a week , and against this can be set the savings in the cost of insurance against explosion and the compensation paid to the men killed and injured .
