# text_id = 1793
# text = The Home Secretary , in addressing his constituents , said much the same as the Prime Minister , namely , that , if it were found that the means test were irksome , or involved anomalies which could not be defended , he would see that the Government , without waiting for the Commission , applied themselves to wiping out the maladministration or misinterpretations or wrong ways of doing it .
