# text_id = 1796
# text = The hon . and learned Member for North Hammersmith ( Mr. Pritt ) made some remarks which I thought — I am not sure that I rightly understood him — might be at any rate construed as suggesting that Judges in this country allowed their decisions to be influenced , not by proper legal considerations or by evidence , but by what they believed to be the wishes of the Executive .
