# text_id = 1804
# text = I said , suppose that Mr. William Graham had succeeded in his Free Trade activities and had made agreements with foreign countries that no additional duties should be laid upon them for five or 10 years , thus barring out the possibility of carrying out a Protectionist policy in this country or the policy of Imperial preference , would the Conservative party have agreed that it was a proper constitutional course ?
