# text_id = 1876
# text = Persons employed in factories are not called upon to examine those places of industry in order to safeguard their work and their lives ; yet in the mining industry men have to make a weekly contribution in order to provide sufficient money to pay their comrades to examine a pit which belongs to someone else so as to ascertain whether it is safe for them to continue their work .
