# text_id = 1910
# text = There never having been a default — because of the necessary sensible commercial effort to keep going — the law steps in and says to the trustee in bankruptcy that it is right in the general interest that whereas the bankrupt could never say " I am walking out on this lease and dropping it without default , " the trustee may say that he is walking out without default .
