# text_id = 1917
# text = I am surprised that the hon . and learned Member for Argyll ( Mr. Macquisten ) started by referring to a lack of proper sense of smell on the part of Pasteur , because it is not long ago since the hon . and learned Member elaborated greatly in this House on the smell of kippers , and he did not find much appreciation for his sense of smell .
