# text_id = 1927
# text = The House will see that we start with the assumption that children shall not take part in entertainments unless they are licensed and then we go on to provide that in certain cases licences shall not be necessary , as when the entertainment is being given for charitable objects , and , subject to certain restrictions , that the children shall not take part in more than six such entertainments .
