# text_id = 1941
# text = If you think it is advisable in the interests of the Colony and of white settlement to offer them land in compensation , and if they will take it voluntarily , by all means let that be done ; but let no man be evicted against his will , and let no British citizen be denied access to the courts of law , which is part of the Morris Carter proposals .
