# text_id = 1962
# text = What I say about the offer made by Mr. Bennett and about the proposals made by all the other Dominion Governments , about which the Secretary of State for the Dominions said nothing , is that they were offers that no serious person , who was not concerned to defend a bad case , would suggest were anything but worthy of consideration , and of the fullest and most serious consideration .
